WEBVTT

NOTE Tube Scan Plan Guide — Normal Beam TCG Calibration
NOTE Language: English (en)

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.980
TCG Calibration for
normal beam inspection.

2
00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:06.080
In this video, you will
learn how to create,

3
00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:09.500
verify, and save a TCG
setup in ScanMaster.

4
00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:13.100
Before you start, prepare six items.

5
00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:16.580
The ScanMaster system,
a normal beam probe,

6
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.380
a calibration block with at
least three FBH reflectors,

7
00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:23.160
the correct material
velocity for the material,

8
00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.840
a stable water path, and
access to teach in mode.

9
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.780
Once everything is ready,
Open the Scan Master Wizard.

10
00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:34.860
On the calibration block,
three FBH standards at

11
00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:37.360
different depths will
work from near to far.

12
00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.180
Standard 1, near.

13
00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:41.160
Standard 2, middle.

14
00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:43.200
Standard 3, far.

15
00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.540
Open the Scan Master Wizard.

16
00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.180
From the main menu, click Teach In.

17
00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:50.200
A new screen image appears,

18
00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:53.440
the instrument window plus
the Setup Toolbox dialog.

19
00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.760
First, set the basic parameters.

20
00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:58.140
Four fields.

21
00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:00.700
1. Material Velocity.

22
00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:02.740
From the material database,

23
00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:04.720
select the material you're inspecting.

24
00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:06.660
2. Range.

25
00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:09.360
Set the range until you see the back wall.

26
00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:11.300
3. Gain.

27
00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:15.520
Verify the response
from the 3/64-inch FBH.

28
00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:17.740
4. Water Path.

29
00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:22.960
Set 76 mm or set the transducer
to surface distance so

30
00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:24.900
the second front
reflection does not appear

31
00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:27.440
between the first front
and first back reflections.

32
00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:32.260
Important. Keep the water
path consistent within plus or

33
00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:35.300
minus one quarter inch
during standardization,

34
00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:38.120
initial scanning, and final evaluation.

35
00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:43.160
Deviation beyond ±¼ inch
requires re-standardization.

36
00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:47.980
Before we set anything else,
understand what TCG is solving.

37
00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:52.020
Before TCG, three identical
flat bottom holes,

38
00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:53.700
three different signal heights.

39
00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:55.620
Closer means stronger.

40
00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:57.120
Farther means weaker.

41
00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:02.960
After TCG, all FBH responses
adjusted to 80% FSH.

42
00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:04.740
One reference level.

43
00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:06.740
One pass-fail criterion.

44
00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.420
Across depth, that is our goal.

45
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:10.600
Let's build it.

46
00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:14.480
Inside the Setup Toolbox,
click the TCG tab.

47
00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:16.620
The TCG table appears.

48
00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:20.480
Before any other action,
verify three checkboxes

49
00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:22.420
on the right side of the TCG tab.

50
00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.100
Active, Visible, Drag.

51
00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.120
All three must be checked.

52
00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:29.760
If drag is off, you cannot drag

53
00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:31.220
the yellow dots in the next steps.

54
00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:34.180
The same action, repeated three times.

55
00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:38.240
Set point 1, near FBH at 80% FSH.

56
00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:42.720
Set point 2, middle FBH at 80% FSH.

57
00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:44.440
Set point 3.

58
00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:47.300
Far FBH at 80% FSH.

59
00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:49.160
Drag yellow dot.

60
00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:51.080
80% FSH.

61
00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:52.980
Save. Three times.

62
00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:56.860
Move the probe to the first
FBH, the near standard.

63
00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:00.800
On the A scan, drag the yellow
dot onto the response peak.

64
00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:05.680
Adjust the gain so the FBH
amplitude reaches 80% FSH.

65
00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:13.540
As you turn Save Point 1.

66
00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:15.900
Click the Save button
on the toolbar setup.

67
00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:17.840
Node 1, Locked.

68
00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:21.760
Move the probe to the second
FBH, the middle standard.

69
00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:25.020
Drag the second yellow dot
onto the new response peak.

70
00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:29.000
Adjust Gain so this peak
also reaches 80% FSH.

71
00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:30.620
Save Point 2.

72
00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:32.540
Node 2, Locked.

73
00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:36.540
Move the probe to the third
FBH, the FAR standard.

74
00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:39.620
Drag the third yellow dot
onto the response peak.

75
00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:42.400
Adjust Gain to 80% FSH.

76
00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:44.160
Save point 3.

77
00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:46.000
Node 3. Locked.

78
00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.220
Three reference points set.

79
00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:50.300
One detail from the guide.

80
00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:52.260
With more than three segments,

81
00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:54.980
scroll boxes appear to the
right of the segment list.

82
00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:58.280
The active segment is marked
with an arrow next to its number.

83
00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:01.220
If your inspection extends
to full part depth,

84
00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:03.920
add a TCG point on the back wall response.

85
00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:06.300
Click the toolbar button to set the

86
00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:08.040
first point before the back wall pulse,

87
00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:10.840
then the second point
after the back wall pulse.

88
00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:13.840
Create at least four points in total to

89
00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:16.840
define the TCG curve through
the back wall response.

90
00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:19.980
Optional. Skip this
step if your inspection

91
00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:22.300
only covers the FBH depth range.

92
00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:24.680
Now save the TCG setup.

93
00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:27.160
Four clicks. 1.

94
00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:29.660
Click the Files tab in the Setup Toolbox.

95
00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:32.700
2. Under TCG, click Save.

96
00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:36.980
3. The UPRDB Navigator dialog opens.

97
00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:39.820
The default file path is
displayed at the bottom.

98
00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:41.960
4. Name the file.

99
00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:45.400
We recommend a naming convention
that includes the Probe Type,

100
00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:47.860
the FBH Size, and the Date.

101
00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:52.700
For example, normal beam
underscore TCG underscore

102
00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:56.660
3/64-inch FBH underscore today's date.

103
00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:00.080
Click Save. TCG setup saved.

104
00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:02.680
Quick checklist before
you run the inspection.

105
00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:04.120
Teach-in opened.

106
00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:06.040
Material velocity set.

107
00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:10.600
Range set. Water path kept within ±¼ inch.

108
00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:14.480
Three FBH responses set to 80% FSH.

109
00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:17.300
Optional back wall points added if needed.

110
00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:19.400
TCG setup saved.

111
00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:21.240
Your TCG is ready.

112
00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:22.700
Run the inspection.

113
00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:25.860
If you need to recalibrate
after a probe change,

114
00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:27.120
a material change,

115
00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:30.540
or any deviation in water
path, return to step 3.

116
00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:33.360
The full Scan Plan documentation is

117
00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:34.840
available in the Scan Plan tab.
